      "id": 1,
      "text": "Roscommon was named after County Roscommon in Ireland, and the county itself was named after that Irish county.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roscommon%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village first settled in 1845 by George Robinson of Detroit, when the Au Sable River cut through a pine forest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://michigan4you.com/history-of-roscommon-michigan/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1873 a Michigan Central Railroad station appeared, turning Roscommon into a railroad town and commerce center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://michigan4you.com/history-of-roscommon-michigan/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The South Branch of the Au Sable River runs through the village, offering kayaking, canoeing, and fishing opportunities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
